{
  "name": "Auto-post RSS items to Bluesky, Mastodon, and Threads with AI summaries",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Auto-post RSS items to Bluesky, Mastodon, and Threads with AI summaries\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Runs automatically every hour.\n2. Fetches the latest items from the RSS feed.\n3. Uses OpenAI to write the post copy and parses it into per-platform fields.\n4. Publishes posts to Bluesky, Mastodon, and Threads via the SocialRobot API.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Install the SocialRobot community node and connect your SocialRobot API credential (API key: socialrobot.io, Scheduler -> API Keys).\n- [ ] Set the RSS feed URL to your own feed.\n- [ ] Select your connected SocialRobot account in each Publish node.\n\n### Customization\n\nEdit the prompt in the AI Summary Generator node, or change the OpenAI model, to tune the tone of the copy. Remove the Publish nodes you do not need to target fewer platforms.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 568
      },
      "id": "ea401822-a948-45e2-92be-cde34d22b417",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
